n:
- This saying might refer to: 

- the transfiguration that follows ({{Matthew 17:1-13|Matthwe 17:1–13}}); 

- the death and resurrection of Jesus Christ ({{Matthew 27:50-53|27:50–53}}; {{Matthew 28:1-10|28:1–10}});

- Pentecost ({{Acts 2:1-47|Acts 2:1–47}}); 

- the destruction of Jerusalem in AD 70 ({{Matthew 24:1-31|Matt 24:1–31}});

- the future second coming of Christ ({{Matthew 24:29-31|24:29–31}}); or

- an ongoing revelation of God’s kingdom, including worldwide evangelism. 

In the fourth view, *coming* would mean "coming in judgment" on sinful Israel. 

- The term Son of Man ({{Matthew 16:27-28|16:27–28}}) creates an *inclusio* (bracketing expression) with {{Matthew 16:13|16:13}}. This creates a unified section ({{Matthew 16:13-28|16:13–28}}) together around the question of who the Son of Man is. He is the Messiah who would first suffer, then be exalted by God, and finally return as Judge.
